We have a smoke detector, ultrasonic detector, sound detector, light sensor, IR sensor, and relay module, and are wiring these into an arduino.

We are using AMD's LeRobot arms, where we'll have a camera and all of our sensors attached to it.

We want to use computer vision to detect potentially hazardous events, and have the robotic arm automatically
adjust its camera to that event to take a picture. This will then be sent to a vlm to get a natural language description, and a point of interest will be saved to a 3D point cloud.

After scanning an area, the user will be able to virtually traverse the area with the points of interest visible in a 3D space. Clicking on a point will show the image that was taken along with its natural language description.
